course: dictionary
lesson: 9920
title: Tandem: two together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tandem is a bicycle built for two riders, sitting one behind the other. «A tandem is a bicycle made for two» tells you this straight away. The word can also be used in the phrase in tandem, and then it means together.
explain: When things happen in tandem, they happen together, at the same time, or people work as a team. «The two sisters jumped in tandem» means they jumped together, at the same moment.
explain: Look at the words around a new word for clues. In «13 riders, 4 full tandems», the word full tells you each tandem carries two riders, so 4 tandems carry 8 riders. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A tandem is a bicycle built for two riders, one behind the other.
fact: «A tandem is a bicycle made for two» has 2 seats and 2 wheels, like an ordinary bicycle.
fact: «In tandem» means together, at the same time, or working as a team.
fact: A tandem jump is a skydive where a beginner jumps with an instructor.
fact: Tandem bike, tandem jump and in tandem with are phrases you can spot in books and in school.
exercise: «A tandem is a bicycle made for two.» What is a tandem? | A bicycle with only one seat | A boat with two sails | A bus for twelve people | *A bicycle built for two riders, one behind the other
exercise: «13 riders, 4 full tandems.» How many riders are on the tandems? | *8 | 13 | 5 | 4
exercise: «The two sisters jumped in tandem.» What does in tandem mean? | *Together, at the same time | Alone, on their own | Angrily, with shouting | Very fast, like a racing car
test: «If some riders are on full tandems and the rest ride a bicycle each, first find how many ride alone.» What should you find first? | The name of the park | *How many ride alone | The colour of the bicycles | How many wheels there are in total
test: A tandem has how many wheels? | 1 | *2 | 3 | 4
exam: «A tandem is a bicycle made for two: it has 2 seats, one behind the other.» How many seats does a tandem have? | *2 | 4 | 6 | 1
